{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIxL0JyZXhpdCUyMFRocm91Z2glMjBUaGUlMjBOb24lMjBQb2xpdGljYWwlMjBHbGFzcyUyMCUyODIwMjElMjkv","type":"movie","name":"Brexit Through The Non Political Glass","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/eLaNSPeKw13gaBI2PL6WhcZjxXV.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/fagPJbwKO0htThaI7NnIC9TdTbg.jpg","description":"On 1 January 2021, the UK's transition period with the EU ended and new rules and regulations were agreed at the last minute. This is a time for reflection on the social phenomenon that is Brexit - which has now become a British trademark world-over, alongside the Royal Family, fish and chips and Sherlock Holmes. Brexit Through The Non-Political Glass puts politicians and public sentiments to one side, and seeks the opinions of non-partisan world-class experts - the scholars and professional advisors who specialize in this very topic; no politicians and propagandists, and no social media and populism; among the experts is Vernon Bogdanor, the Oxford tutor of former British prime minister David Cameron, who was consulted before the referendum was offered to the nation; you will hear what his advice was.\n\nRated U · Released 13 Oct 2021 · Slovenia, United Kingdom · Language: English · 85 min\nStudio: Perfo Production, Partisan Media\n\nOn your server — Audio: English · Subtitle files: English","releaseInfo":"2021","genres":["Documentary","Hollywood"],"runtime":"85 min","cast":["Tim Bale","Catherine Barnard","Vernon Bogdanor","Vida Breže"],"director":["Nina Kojima"],"released":"2021-10-13T00:00:00.000Z","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Nina Kojima","character":"Director"},{"name":"Tim Bale","character":"Himself"},{"name":"Catherine Barnard","character":"Herself","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/nRpJYCOE6iRZUYjyIsggmam9dvn.jpg"},{"name":"Vernon Bogdanor","character":"Himself"},{"name":"Vida Breže","character":"Herself","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/9tRcaSF